{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"b7c7c135-fdbf-497a-a147-6656395fdef2","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Summary of Cause \u0026 Fix\n\n#### Cause\nIn `posthog_flutter`, mobile session replay requires the application widget tree to be wrapped inside [`PostHogWidget`](file:///tmp/h-VnoQ72/lib/legacy_app.dart#L13-L23). `PostHogWidget` houses the `RepaintBoundary`, change detector, masking calculations, and the screenshot capture pipeline that captures frames and delivers snapshots to the native SDK.\n\n- In [`lib/legacy_app.dart`](file:///tmp/h-VnoQ72/lib/legacy_app.dart), `MaterialApp` was properly wrapped inside `PostHogWidget`.\n- In [`lib/new_app.dart`](file:///tmp/h-VnoQ72/lib/new_app.dart), `NewApp` directly returned `MaterialApp.router(...)` without `PostHogWidget`.\n\nCustom events and screen tracking continued to work because `Analytics.init()` and `PosthogObserver()` were active, but session replay frames were never captured.\n\n#### Fix\nWrapped `MaterialApp.router(...)` inside `PostHogWidget` in [`lib/new_app.dart`](file:///tmp/h-VnoQ72/lib/new_app.dart). Documented the findings and fix in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-VnoQ72/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":129.549316,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":207524,"output_tokens":3013,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":551447,"total_tokens":210537}}}
